1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 28=

4
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:02,840
Your Majesty.

5
00:01:04,159 --> 00:01:05,000
What is it?

6
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:06,280
Your Majesty.

7
00:01:07,079 --> 00:01:07,880
Zhang Yuying

8
00:01:08,119 --> 00:01:09,000
has hanged herself.

9
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:13,800
She will not be buried
in the imperial mausoleum.

10
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,880
See to it.

11
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,160
Yes, Your Majesty.

12
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,160
(Lishui Pavilion)

13
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:54,720
Greetings, Prince Ning.

14
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:55,880
No need for formalities.

15
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,920
I heard

16
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,760
Zhang Yuying passed away.

17
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,560
I was thinking

18
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,120
of copying some sutras for her

19
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,239
to see her off.

20
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,799
If you truly mean to pray for her soul,

21
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,719
I doubt she'd dare accept it.

22
00:02:21,639 --> 00:02:22,919
Your Highness,

23
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,879
I don't understand what you mean.

24
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:27,800
Some things in the palace

25
00:02:28,159 --> 00:02:30,199
are better left unknown.

26
00:02:34,039 --> 00:02:35,479
As for what happened to Consort Shu,

27
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,080
I asked no questions

28
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,639
because she brought it on herself.

29
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,000
As for what happened to Consort Chen,

30
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:43,639
I asked no questions either,

31
00:02:44,319 --> 00:02:46,159
because she'd done evil for too long.

32
00:02:46,919 --> 00:02:49,039
Some festering sores must be cut out

33
00:02:49,639 --> 00:02:51,280
before the rot reaches the bone.

34
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:59,439
But if that blade keeps cutting,

35
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:02,400
it'll eventually hurt the wrong people.

36
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:09,120
Noble Consort Hui,

37
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,479
I don't know what you're really after.

38
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,439
But I am His Majesty's own uncle.

39
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,199
I may not see everything,

40
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:17,280
but I can tell this much:

41
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,960
His Majesty's feelings for you

42
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,080
are genuine.

43
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,439
I'll remember

44
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,599
your counsel, Your Highness.

45
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,600
None of the calming remedies

46
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,600
from the Imperial Medical Bureau

47
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:38,720
work as well as this herbal sachet
you made.

48
00:04:40,279 --> 00:04:41,800
Only its scent

49
00:04:42,839 --> 00:04:45,879
lets me sleep a few hours at best.

50
00:04:48,759 --> 00:04:50,079
All these years,

51
00:04:51,519 --> 00:04:52,680
in the harem,

52
00:04:53,879 --> 00:04:56,720
only you could stand beside me.

53
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,439
I owe you the title of Empress.

54
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,079
I've owed it to you far too long.

55
00:05:13,399 --> 00:05:15,000
Do you remember, Your Majesty,

56
00:05:15,879 --> 00:05:18,120
the late Empress's death anniversary
is approaching?

57
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,279
I know.

58
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,120
After we honor Roujia,

59
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,319
I'll issue the decree.

60
00:05:29,519 --> 00:05:32,360
You only noticed me

61
00:05:32,879 --> 00:05:34,399
because I stood in her shadow.

62
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:38,079
The late Empress was without equal.

63
00:05:39,279 --> 00:05:41,720
I can't bring myself to take her place.

64
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:44,360
If Your Majesty truly cares for me,

65
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,399
then please

66
00:05:47,319 --> 00:05:49,079
don't mention this again.

67
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,600
Su.

68
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,839
You've changed.

69
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:12,600
When you used to give me medicine,

70
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:18,240
you'd smile and call me Che.

71
00:06:20,279 --> 00:06:21,600
Back then,

72
00:06:23,319 --> 00:06:25,319
there was light in your eyes.

73
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,279
You'd pout.

74
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,399
You'd laugh.

75
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,160
Now,

76
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:35,240
you sit right in front of me,

77
00:06:36,279 --> 00:06:37,839
yet I feel

78
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,879
as though you're

79
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,120
so far away.

80
00:06:42,879 --> 00:06:44,120
So far away.

81
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,800
Your Majesty,
you're reading too much into it.

82
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:48,000
I'm still me.

83
00:06:48,319 --> 00:06:49,480
I've never changed.

84
00:06:59,519 --> 00:07:01,000
Please get some rest, Your Majesty.

85
00:07:02,199 --> 00:07:03,439
Get well.

86
00:07:03,639 --> 00:07:05,519
In a few days,
you'll need to visit Guizhen Cottage.

87
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,680
I'll take my leave.

88
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:50,107
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

89
00:07:50,241 --> 00:07:53,854
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

90
00:07:54,089 --> 00:07:56,688
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

91
00:07:56,725 --> 00:07:59,005
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

92
00:07:59,052 --> 00:08:02,881
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

93
00:08:03,283 --> 00:08:06,636
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

94
00:08:07,563 --> 00:08:11,076
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

95
00:08:11,576 --> 00:08:14,143
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

96
00:08:14,269 --> 00:08:16,302
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

97
00:08:16,369 --> 00:08:20,146
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

98
00:08:20,496 --> 00:08:24,829
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

99
00:08:25,052 --> 00:08:28,559
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

100
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:31,593
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

101
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:37,274
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

102
00:08:37,314 --> 00:08:40,328
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

103
00:08:40,369 --> 00:08:46,377
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

104
00:08:47,044 --> 00:08:53,999
♪The past has faded away♪

105
00:08:53,999 --> 00:08:57,531
♪The past has faded away♪
